{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01051",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.25,
      "end_seconds": 4.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "Good afternoon, how are you today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.97,
      "end_seconds": 7.19,
      "duration_seconds": 1.22,
      "text": "what's the problem?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 9.12,
      "end_seconds": 17.12,
      "duration_seconds": 8.0,
      "text": "Um, so... sharp pain in the upper right of my tummy. That's why I came."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.68,
      "end_seconds": 23.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "How long has it been like this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 24.26,
      "end_seconds": 26.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "for two weeks, I'd say"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 28.76,
      "end_seconds": 37.73,
      "duration_seconds": 8.97,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 39.18,
      "end_seconds": 59.28,
      "duration_seconds": 20.1,
      "text": "it settles a little with lying still. Moderate, I'd say. My sister suggested writing things down, but I forgot. There's bloating as well. About bloating, it feels severe to me. And nausea after meals as well, um, since yesterday"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 60.22,
      "end_seconds": 63.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "any a bit of vomiting as well?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 65.49,
      "end_seconds": 66.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.21,
      "text": "yes, actually"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 72.26,
      "end_seconds": 80.1,
      "duration_seconds": 7.84,
      "text": "have you had sharp pain in the upper right of your tummy before or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 81.76,
      "end_seconds": 87.44,
      "duration_seconds": 5.68,
      "text": "I had a similar thing last winter it went away"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 90.86,
      "end_seconds": 96.33,
      "duration_seconds": 5.47,
      "text": "And what about pale stools, black stools, fever or dark urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 96.96,
      "end_seconds": 99.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "Nope, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.96,
      "end_seconds": 104.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "have you had any weight loss or yellow eyes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.78,
      "end_seconds": 110.69,
      "duration_seconds": 4.91,
      "text": "No weight loss or yellow eyes none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 111.23,
      "end_seconds": 114.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "how about your heart any problems like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 116.31,
      "end_seconds": 118.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "no, that's been fine"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 120.13,
      "end_seconds": 122.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "before we go further, any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 124.6,
      "end_seconds": 128.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "No, I've never reacted to to anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 140.82,
      "end_seconds": 143.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "let's run through your medicines"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 144.94,
      "end_seconds": 148.6,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "Atorvastatin, 20 milligrams, maybe, at night"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 150.07,
      "end_seconds": 154.25,
      "duration_seconds": 4.18,
      "text": "Did you happen to bring the box or the paperwork?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 156.3,
      "end_seconds": 163.91,
      "duration_seconds": 7.61,
      "text": "no, it's at home. Allopurinol. I take it it 100 milligrams, once a day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.38,
      "end_seconds": 168.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.36,
      "text": "how long has that been going on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 169.39,
      "end_seconds": 170.78,
      "duration_seconds": 1.39,
      "text": "About two months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 172.02,
      "end_seconds": 175.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "alright, are you on your own at home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 176.76,
      "end_seconds": 180.11,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "I live with my elderly mother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 181.48,
      "end_seconds": 183.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "Do you do any exercise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 188.54,
      "end_seconds": 191.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "I swim twice a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.56,
      "end_seconds": 196.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "so, what line of work are you in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 196.82,
      "end_seconds": 202.45,
      "duration_seconds": 5.63,
      "text": "I'm a bus driver, so I sit for long hours."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 203.11,
      "end_seconds": 206.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "anything in your past medical history I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 208.02,
      "end_seconds": 211.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "I've got high cholesterol yes gout"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 213.13,
      "end_seconds": 218.84,
      "duration_seconds": 5.71,
      "text": "Yes, high cholesterol and gout are known to us, good to have that clear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.7,
      "end_seconds": 236.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "I'll note down your vital signs first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 248.91,
      "end_seconds": 251.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "okay, this won't take long.."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 263.78,
      "end_seconds": 272.49,
      "duration_seconds": 8.71,
      "text": "Okay: pulse is 70 beats a a minute, saturation 97 percent, temp 36.6 degrees, blood pressure 116 over 72."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 273.77,
      "end_seconds": 275.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.38,
      "text": "Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 275.81,
      "end_seconds": 279.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "They help me see the whole picture, more shortly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.76,
      "end_seconds": 283.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "Alright shall I start the the examination?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 285.18,
      "end_seconds": 288.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "I'll listen to to your chest now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 303.57,
      "end_seconds": 312.35,
      "duration_seconds": 8.78,
      "text": "There is tenderness under the right ribs when you breathe in and and no yellowing of the eyes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 316.11,
      "end_seconds": 333.3,
      "duration_seconds": 17.19,
      "text": "good, you can sit up again so where does that leave us? It fits best with biliary colic from gallstones the reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together. Peptic ulcer is still possible"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 335.31,
      "end_seconds": 338.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.21,
      "text": "do you think it's something serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 343.26,
      "end_seconds": 351.03,
      "duration_seconds": 7.77,
      "text": "nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like biliary colic from gallstones but I'd like to confirm"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 367.36,
      "end_seconds": 400.02,
      "duration_seconds": 32.66,
      "text": "I think an ultrasound of the tummy makes sense here, for right upper quadrant pain i'm going to order liver blood tests, for upper abdominal pain i'm going to put you on diclofenac, 50 milligrams, three times a day if needed, for three days it's for gallbladder pain it's a commonly used medicine and most people tolerate it well keep meals small and low in fat until we have the scan"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 400.85,
      "end_seconds": 421.85,
      "duration_seconds": 21.0,
      "text": "a short walk every day even twenty minutes will help more than you'd think. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit so we can settle the dose. I'll want another look after the ultrasound. Anything else on your mind before you go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 422.81,
      "end_seconds": 424.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "alright thanks take care"
    }
  ]
}